@*
    Task 11.1. Two edits.

    (1) HttpContext.Current.Request.QueryString["ReturnUrl"] -> Context.Request.Query["ReturnUrl"].
        System.Web's static HttpContext.Current has no ASP.NET Core counterpart; RazorPageBase
        exposes the ambient HttpContext as `Context`, which is the substitution tasks 7.3 and 8.4
        made across all 518 views. The StringValues -> string conversion is subtle; see the
        comment on the local below.

    (2) The static asset reference is UNCHANGED, and that is the point of runtime deferral
        10.x-1: ~/Plugins/ExternalAuth.Facebook/Content/facebookstyles.css 404'd until task 11.1
        widened NopStaticFileProvider's allow-list, because task 7.4 replaced System.Web's
        serve-the-application-root static handler with an allow-list that had no Plugins/ entry.
        This stylesheet is the ONLY source of the login button's size, background image and
        colour - a.facebook-btn has no text - so a 404 here renders a zero-size empty anchor.
        Invisible control, no error anywhere. Asserted over real HTTP by
        Nop.Web.SmokeTests.PluginStaticAssetTests.

    Layout = "" is 3.90's and is honoured by ASP.NET Core: this is a fragment rendered into the
    storefront login page through the Html.Action bridge (IExternalAuthenticationMethod's
    action/controller/RouteValueDictionary triple, deferral 7.3-1). The @using Nop.Web.Framework.UI
    that 3.90 declared here is now in Views/_ViewImports.cshtml along with the rest of the deleted
    web.config's <namespaces>, so it is dropped rather than duplicated.
*@
@{
    Layout = "";

    Html.AddCssFileParts("~/Plugins/ExternalAuth.Facebook/Content/facebookstyles.css");

    //Assigned to a `string` local ON PURPOSE. Request.Query[...] is StringValues; its IMPLICIT
    //STRING CONVERSION yields null for an absent key, whereas StringValues.ToString() yields
    //string.Empty. Only the first reproduces NameValueCollection's indexer, and the difference is
    //observable: RouteUrl omits a null route value but emits "?ReturnUrl=" for an empty one.
    string returnUrl = Context.Request.Query["ReturnUrl"];
}
<div class="facebook-login-block">
    <div class="buttons">
        <a href="@Url.RouteUrl("Plugin.ExternalAuth.Facebook.Login", new { ReturnUrl = returnUrl })" class="facebook-btn"></a>
    </div>
</div>
